    "body": "The maintainer asked for this work in chat on 2026-11-17, with a screenshot of the \"Report a problem\" dialog of Solidcraft (his own CAD program):\n\n> there is also this nice report a problem dialog reachble from there.\n\nThe priority is now `P4` for that reason.\n\nWhat the reference dialog has:\n- A \"Report a bug\" button in the top bar that opens it.\n- A type selection: Bug, Feature, Question.\n- A title field and a description field.\n- A check box to include the open project file, off by default, with the file name and its size, and a sentence that says who can see the file.\n- A screenshot of the 3D view, with a preview and a \"Retake screenshot\" button.\n- A check box to attach the log.\n- Close and Send buttons.\n\nOpen question for the maintainer, before code: where \"Send\" sends the report. The choices are a GitHub issue that opens in the browser with the text filled in (no attachment upload, no account data in the program), or a service that receives the report with its attachments. The rule of issue #1749 applies: the user's files stay private unless the user sends them.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
